---
import LegalContact from '../components/LegalContact.astro';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How PayFlow Africa handles personal information collected through the payflowafrica.com website."
  updated="7 October 2026"
>
  <p class="legal__note">
    PayFlow Africa is an early-stage company and this notice covers this website only. We will update it before any
    PayFlow Africa product handles customer or employee data.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    PayFlow Africa (“we”, “us”) is an early-stage company developing payroll and HR software. This notice explains how
    we handle personal information collected through payflowafrica.com (the “website”).
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Information you choose to send us.</strong> If you request early access or contact us, we receive the details
      you provide: typically your name, work email address, organisation, role, organisation size, country and any message
      you include.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider processes standard technical data,
      such as IP addresses, browser type and the pages requested, to deliver the website and protect it from abuse.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use analytics tools, advertising trackers or marketing cookies on this website, and the website itself does
    not set cookies. Our hosting and security provider may set strictly necessary security cookies in some circumstances,
    for example to protect the website against automated abuse.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>We use the information you send us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>respond to your enquiry;</li>
    <li>manage the early-access list and contact you about PayFlow Africa early access;</li>
    <li>understand the payroll and HR needs of organisations interested in the product.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information or use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We share personal information only with service providers that help us run the website and communicate with you, such
    as our hosting provider and our email or form-processing provider, and only as needed for those purposes. We may also
    disclose information where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep early-access and enquiry details while the early-access programme is running, or until you ask us to delete
    them, whichever comes first.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us at any time to access, correct or delete the information we hold about you, or to stop contacting you.
    Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under local data protection law.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable steps to protect the information we hold. No method of transmission or storage is completely
    secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Where information is processed</h2>
  <p>Our service providers may process information in countries other than your own.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This website is intended for organisations and professionals and is not directed at children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>We will update this notice as PayFlow Africa develops and change the “last updated” date when we do.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <LegalContact topic="this notice or your information" />
</LegalLayout>
